<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s284S">Well the case <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w1">above</span> is exactly the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w2">same</span>! The <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w8">three</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w7">things</span> mentioned, the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w3"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s284m5">blood</span> and <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s284m4">pus</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w6">and the other</span> two, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w15">are</span> all <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w14">parts</span> of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w12">glass</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w13">full</span> of something <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w9">wet</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s284p10">and</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w11">flowing</span>. <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s284p18">When</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w16">three</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w17">appear</span> then we can <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w29">say</span> that the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w22">glass</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w23">full</span> of a thing which is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w19">wet</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s284p20">and</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w21">flowing</span> is acting as a basis, and that <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w27">three</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w26">different</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w25">ways of appearing</span> are being <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w28">displayed</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s284w24">upon</span> it.</span>
</div>
