<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex (independent Tibetan-first proposal). Both wet/flowing and glass/full descriptions, and all three gsum occurrences, are distinguished. rnag khrag is the blood-and-pus compound, whose members cross in English. sogs owns only “and the other”; the supplied number “two” remains unpaired. steng owns “upon”, while the expanded basis wording remains unpaired. Unresolved connective and grammatical content is omitted, not asserted null. No new erratum is proposed.</div>
